  "historical_output_text": " The Jet_STREAM pattern, for our weather patterns to talk simply, think \"fast, high, fast\" and you've almost captured its meaning. Picture high in Earth, about nine kilometers above our level ground and a vast band stretching from the Atlantic across Canada into the Western Atlantic is moving very fast—hustly as you or maybe as quickly a train moving on the straight tracks.\n\nImagine this high-altiude road for airplanes has its main direction going East and this path is not fixed in time, rather the jet_stream dances with its winds, moving in loops that can twist around like cogs, sometimes going further north and even reaching as low latidute regions, sometimes going much lower down in the air and moving more slowly in places like North Dakota, but the average flow remains eastward, very fast!\n\nWhen warm air moves towards cold air",
